Use algebraic working in each part.","contextKind":"ABSTRACT","contextDescription":"An algebraic quadratic equation is given directly with no applied situation.","construct":"QUADRATIC_EQUATION_RATIONAL_ROOTS_BY_FACTORISING","parameters":[{"symbol":"a","value":2},{"symbol":"r1","value":-3},{"symbol":"r2","value":2}],"responseKind":"CONSTRUCTED","options":[],"answerKey":null,"distractors":[],"answers":[{"label":"a","prompt":"Work out the factorised form of the equation.","commandTerm":"work out","marks":2,"markPoints":[{"kind":"METHOD","marks":1,"criterion":"Rearranges or groups the terms correctly to obtain a factorised quadratic expression."},{"kind":"ACCURACY","marks":1,"criterion":"Gives the correct factorised equation, 2(x + 3)(x - 2) = 0."}],"finalAnswer":"2(x + 3)(x - 2) = 0","numericValue":null,"decimalPlaces":null,"targetKind":"NOT_MACHINE_CHECKABLE","targetCode":null,"verdictValue":null,"comparisonLeft":null,"comparisonOperator":null,"comparisonRight":null,"comparisonHolds":null,"notCheckableReason":"A factorised algebraic expression must be assessed symbolically rather than as one numeric value.","arithmeticExpression":null},{"label":"b","prompt":"Work out the lesser root of the equation.","commandTerm":"work out","marks":2,"markPoints":[{"kind":"METHOD","marks":1,"criterion":"Uses the factorised equation to set the appropriate factor equal to zero."},{"kind":"ACCURACY","marks":1,"criterion":"Obtains the lesser root x = -3."}],"finalAnswer":"x = -3","numericValue":"-3","decimalPlaces":0,"targetKind":"QUANTITY","targetCode":"LESSER_ROOT","verdictValue":null,"comparisonLeft":null,"comparisonOperator":null,"comparisonRight":null,"comparisonHolds":null,"notCheckableReason":null,"arithmeticExpression":null},{"label":"c","prompt":"Calculate the greater root of the equation.","commandTerm":"calculate","marks":2,"markPoints":[{"kind":"METHOD","marks":1,"criterion":"Uses the remaining factor in the factorised equation and sets it equal to zero."},{"kind":"ACCURACY","marks":1,"criterion":"Obtains the greater root x = 2."}],"finalAnswer":"x = 2","numericValue":"2","decimalPlaces":0,"targetKind":"QUANTITY","targetCode":"GREATER_ROOT","verdictValue":null,"comparisonLeft":null,"comparisonOperator":null,"comparisonRight":null,"comparisonHolds":null,"notCheckableReason":null,"arithmeticExpression":null}],"workingOutline":["Rewrite 2x^2 + 2x - 12 as 2(x^2 + x - 6).","Factorise x^2 + x - 6 as (x + 3)(x - 2), giving 2(x + 3)(x - 2) = 0.","Set x + 3 = 0 to obtain the lesser root x = -3.","Set x - 2 = 0 to obtain the greater root x = 2."],"creditLevels":[],"rationale":"The item requires the learner to factorise a quadratic equation and then read both rational roots from the factors. The three parts preserve the solve sequence while separately eliciting the factorised equation, the lesser root and the greater root. The values a = 2, r1 = -3 and r2 = 2 produce integer coefficients and are not among the excluded parameter sets.","usesStimulusValues":[],"supportingConceptStableIds":["math.alg.quadratics"]}}
